From: cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-vayu: enable IPA

Without IPA there is no network port for the modem and ModemManager
rejects the device with "Failed to find a net port in the QMI modem", even
though QMI probing over QRTR works.

We use qcom,gsi-loader = "self" with the ipa_fws.mdt extracted from the
stock/LineageOS vendor partition. The "modem" mode was tried first and is
not good enough: the driver gets as far as "received modem running event"
but the modem never sends the ipa-setup-ready signal and the setup never
completes.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi	2026-08-02 20:27:32.534942164 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi	2026-08-02 20:27:32.545776414 +0200
@@ -500,6 +500,13 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&ipa {
+	qcom,gsi-loader = "self";
+	memory-region = <&ipa_fw_mem>;
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/Xiaomi/vayu/ipa_fws.mdt";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &spi17 {
 	status = "okay";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&qup_spi17_default>;
